Next.js serves this directory at the site root.

It is empty and tracked deliberately: the web Dockerfile copies it, and git
does not track empty directories, so without this file a fresh checkout has no
apps/web/public and the image build fails on COPY. That is exactly what broke
CI while it worked locally.

Anything that must be served at a literal path — favicon.ico, robots overrides,
verification files for Search Console — goes here. Fonts do not: next/font
hashes and serves them from /_next/static.
